cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Linux-PERFORMANCE in your research, please cite it using the following metadata."
title: "Linux-PERFORMANCE: A Modular Framework for Automated Optimization, Hardening and Engineering-Grade Setup of Linux Mint"
abstract: >
  Linux-PERFORMANCE is an engineering-focused automation framework designed to
  install, configure, optimize, and secure Linux Mint systems in a reproducible,
  modular, and scientifically transparent way. It provides structured pipelines,
  performance modules, security hardening, and documentation suitable for
  research, reproducibility studies, and engineering workflows.

